//
// SmolVLA compile-only smoke test: builds every SigLIP vision ELF through the
// AIR -> AIE -> aiecc -> Peano pipeline. No NPU dispatch, no HuggingFace
// download, no lerobot import — so it runs anywhere the toolchain is installed.
//
// Covers the three fused multi-launch ELFs (vit_ln_qkv, flash_attn,
// vit_o_ffn), the post-LayerNorm and the connector projection.
//
// NOT CI-triggered by design: the filename OMITS "peano", so the CI peano suite
// (`lit --filter "peano"`) does not collect it — llama32_1b's compile lit is the
// bf16 CI signal and this example shares the same shared/builders + shared/infra
// assembly. Run on demand:
//   lit -v programming_examples/llms/smolvla/run_npu2_compile.lit
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_compile
// RUN: cd test_peano_compile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: Compilation passed.
